# Conformance probe pack for gate blocks (spec 0.17) under six-bit armor
# (spec 0.14, ruling 14 of 0.17). Fixed `bits` layout, most significant bit
# first, read and written as armored text. Public. No kinds. Exercises: a
# block held by its gate, and one that does not hold, in the armored text; a
# gate that lies after its field and whose locator extends the text by one
# character; an `optional` field of a held block that counts toward `L` only
# when it is written; a gate whose bit lies beyond the bits the text carries
# does not hold.
#
#   bits 0-5     n, outside any block (the first character)
#   bits 6-11    x, in the block (the second character)
#   bit  12      the gate of x and y: they are there when the bit is 1
#   bits 13-23   y, in the block, optional
format       conformance-gates-armor
version      0.17.0
distribution public
source       "goat-transformers spec/engine-spec.md (synthetic probe format, no external standard)"
uses         probe
wire         bits
word_bytes   1
bit_order    msb
armor        sixbit
field   probe.n   0:0:6    uint
if      0:12:1  1
  field probe.x   0:6:6    uint
  field probe.y   0:13:11  uint  optional
end
